# The LittleFS payload is uploaded byte-for-byte by `pio run -t uploadfs` and
# parsed by hand-rolled firmware that splits on '\n'. A CRLF checkout on Windows
# would leave a trailing '\r' on the last field of every row — turning a logo
# name into "RA_DR.png\r", which LittleFS cannot open. Keep it LF everywhere.
Esp32InternetRadio/data/stations.csv text eol=lf

# The logos are raw RGB565 pixel dumps, not text. Git's binary detection would
# almost certainly get this right on its own — 16,928 bytes of image data will
# contain NULs — but "almost certainly" is how the line above became necessary,
# and a single logo mangled by CRLF conversion would be a torn picture on the
# screen with nothing in any log to explain it.
Esp32InternetRadio/data/logos/*.565 binary
